#!/usr/bin/env python3
# dojo-summary: check a lab against your Dojo WAN org: dojo check N (0-9)
"""dojo check N: asks the Dojo WAN API what your org looks like now and says what matches.

It reads the result (the objects in your org and the Junos config each gateway would get), not your
files, using your own token, the same calls `curl` makes. Lab 6 also reads Terraform's state list, and
labs 8 and 9 run `terraform plan` to prove the code and the org agree.

    dojo check           list the labs
    dojo check 4         check lab 4   (lab4 and c4 mean the same)
"""
